{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"## Human intervention needed\n\nThe automated job for `org.jctools:jctools-core:4.0.3` failed (`test_generation_failed`). Preserved work is available at [the preservation branch](https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fvjovanov%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9253-library-update-request-org.jctools-jctools-core-4.0.3-c9283bf8).\n\nThe likely failing stage is post-generation metadata repair/native runtime verification. Although coverage tracing reported 18/19 dynamic accesses (94.74%), the final native test ran six tests and five failed during JCTools class initialization. `org.jctools.util.UnsafeAccess.fieldOffset()` calls `Class.getDeclaredField()` for unregistered fields: `_kvs` (`NonBlockingHashMap` and `NonBlockingIdentityHashMap`), `_chm` (`NonBlockingHashMapLong`), and `producerNode` (`BaseLinkedQueueProducerNodeRef`). The existing `consumerIndex` and `producerIndex` registrations are conditioned on target classes that are reached too late. The repair attempt was blocked before it could write metadata or rerun Gradle verification.\n\nInspect `logs/org.jctools:jctools-core:4.0.3/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-08-15T18-38-14-965695Z.log`, `logs/org.jctools:jctools-core:4.0.3/metadata-fix/codex.log`, and `logs/org.jctools:jctools-core:4.0.3/post-gen/pi-post-gen-2026-08-15T18-36-55-111487Z.log`.\n\n1. Check out the preserved branch and retain the generated queue/map/serialization tests.\n2. Update `metadata/org.jctools/jctools-core/4.0.3/reachability-metadata.json` with the missing field registrations, using an early `org.jctools.util.UnsafeAccess` condition; also verify whether `_val_1` is required.\n3. Run `./gradlew test -Pcoordinates=org.jctools:jctools-core:4.0.3`, iterate on any further native-image registration failures, then regenerate/verify stats before opening a PR."}}
